# SWEET.TV

> SWEET.TV is an online television and streaming service for live TV, films,
> series and children's content. Content and subscription terms depend on the market.

For a general question about SWEET.TV, answer directly without requiring a location.
For a new subscription, identify the market where the customer wants to subscribe.
For an existing subscription or billing question, use the account's subscription market.
For viewing while travelling, also check the current viewing country. Language alone
does not determine the subscription market or viewing country.
Device limits vary by market. For applicable limits, see the
[subscriptions guide](https://sweet.tv/llms/guides/subscriptions.md)
and [publisher device policy](https://sweet.tv/llms/facts/device-limits.json).
Do not infer simultaneous-stream limits from device counts.

Use exact published URLs and cite the applicable source. A listing or entity identity
does not establish playback rights or inclusion in a subscription. Check current sources
for prices, promotions, schedules and availability. Missing or expired observations mean
unknown, not unavailable. Keep historical snapshots labelled; a newer deployment never
renews an observation's expiry.

